Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The container parser and writer, the lossless (VP8L) decoder and encoder,
the alpha (ALPH) coding, the animation compositor and encoder and the
colour conversion are original implementations written from RFC 9649 (WebP
Image Format) and ITU-R BT.601. They are not translations of, and do not
derive from, any other WebP implementation's source; none was read (not
libwebp, not image-rs's image-webp, not any other), and none is run by the
tests. The lossy (VP8) bitstream is decoded and encoded by rivet-vp8, this
project's own clean-room VP8 codec written from RFC 6386.
docs/PROVENANCE.md records each source and every point where the RFC is
silent or ambiguous and what decided it.

The decoder is checked against Google's public WebP test files and gallery
images (libwebp-test-data and the WebP gallery), used as data and not
distributed here.

